# ---- Generated output ----
# Figures are generated artifacts (no current script reproduces them).
# Delete the lines below if you want to version specific figures.
#
# ANCHORED to the repo root. Unanchored, `figures/` matches a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed frontend/src/components/figures/ --
# the chart components -- when it was added. This rule is about the exported
# PDFs at the top level and nothing else.
/figures/
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.svg

# ---- Data artifacts (keep the small, curated CSVs tracked, ignore scratch) ----
*.parquet
*.feather
*.pkl
*.h5
*.hdf5
*.csv
# ...but keep the datasets the project actually needs in the repo.
#
# nhanes_adolescent.csv is the one the deployed app reads: the study's analytic
# cohort, ~700 rows and ~100 KB, derived from the raw merge by Backend/cohort.py.
# It is committed rather than built on deploy so production never depends on the
# 17 MB raw file being present -- see the LFS note below.
#
# nhanes_analytic.csv is that raw 412-column merge. It is tracked through GIT LFS
# (see .gitattributes), not ignored: it is the provenance for everything else and
# belongs under version control, but at 17 MB it does not belong in the ordinary
# object history. Nothing at runtime reads it -- only `python Backend/cohort.py`
# does, when rebuilding the cohort -- so a checkout that never ran `git lfs pull`
# still runs the site correctly.
#
# nhanes.csv is the previous curated 18-column demo slice, superseded by the
# cohort but kept for reference and for the older figures.
!Data/data.csv
!Data/nhanes.csv
!Data/nhanes_adolescent.csv
!Data/nhanes_analytic.csv

# ---- Django ----
# Local run log. The host has no persistent disk, so this is never shared state.
# Committing it would bake a stale database into the deployed image.
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite3-journal
*.sqlite3-wal
*.sqlite3-shm

# ---- Environment / secrets ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Security scan output (nuclei etc. -- don't broadcast findings) ----
nuclei*
*.nuclei
.nuclei/
.nuclei-templates/

# ---- IDE / editors ----
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.vscode/
*.code-workspace
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.claude

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Studio run-log (local lab notebook; free tier has no persistent disk)
Backend/studio_runs.db

# Frontend (Vite + React + TypeScript). The bundle is built on deploy from
# source (see render.yaml), never committed -- a checked-in build can drift from
# the source it was made from without anything failing to say so.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/node_modules/.tmp/
